<div class="wrap page-head"><h1>Give</h1><p class="lede">The Campaign to Sustain builds a monthly revenue stream and an endowment so the Foundation can keep bringing the Churches together long after its founder. The goal is $5,000 a month and a $100,000 endowment.</p></div>
<section class="band white">
  <div class="wrap two-col">
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="kicker">What's next</p>
      <h2>An institute for advanced studies in ecumenism.</h2>
      <p>Since 1997 the Foundation's grass-roots conferences and pilgrimages have given lay people and clergy a place to learn the light of the East and pray together for the unity Christ asked for at the Last Supper. For its thirtieth anniversary the Foundation is expanding that mission: it is in discussions with the <a class="textlink" href="https://likoudislegacy.com/">Likoudis Legacy Foundation</a> about creating an educational and ecumenical institute with accredited advanced studies in ecumenical theology.</p>
      <p>The dialogue has produced real progress, in the statements of Ravenna, Chieti, and Alexandria. The institute would equip a younger generation of ecumenically minded, faith-based students to receive those statements and contribute to the next ones. Now is the time to continue the grass-roots effort even more fervently, which the official dialogues have encouraged.</p>
      <blockquote class="quote" style="margin:1.5rem 0">“We are all invited to overcome the scandal of the divisions that unfortunately still exist and to nurture the desire for unity for which the Lord Jesus prayed and gave his life.”<cite>Pope Leo XIV at Nicaea, November 2025. Jack Figel met him face to face at the July 2025 pilgrimage.</cite></blockquote>
      <p>Whether you can give $25, $100, or $500, your gift helps the Foundation expand its mission and explore founding the institute.</p>
    </div>
    <img src="/images/francis-icon.jpg" alt="Jack Figel presents an icon to Pope Francis" style="width:100%;aspect-ratio:3/2;object-fit:cover" loading="lazy">
